Third-party programs shipped in container images, not linked into KloudChat code
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

FFmpeg (ffmpeg, ffprobe) — https://ffmpeg.org
  Image: kloudchat-media (apps/media/Dockerfile)
  Licence: GNU LGPL 2.1 or later; this Debian build also enables GPL components, so the
  binaries as distributed are under the GNU GPL 2 or later.
  How it is used: installed as Debian's unmodified `ffmpeg` package and run only as a
  separate program by apps/media/server.py, which talks to it through its command line. No
  KloudChat code links, embeds or modifies FFmpeg. The licence texts and the source offer
  ship in the image under /usr/share/doc/ffmpeg/ and /usr/share/doc/libav*/ (copyright);
  the corresponding source is available from Debian (`apt-get source ffmpeg`,
  https://sources.debian.org/src/ffmpeg/).

Korean fonts fetched into the API image at build, used to set words on generated pictures
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Black Han Sans, Do Hyeon, Jua, Gaegu, Nanum Brush Script, BM YEONSUNG — Google Fonts
  Image: kloudchat-api (apps/api/Dockerfile), /usr/share/fonts/truetype/kloudchat/
  Licence: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (commercial use and bundling allowed; the fonts are not
  sold on their own). Each family's licence text is stored beside its files as <file>.OFL.txt.
  How it is used: opened by services/image_text.py to draw text onto a picture; nothing is
  modified or renamed.

PaperBanana style guide (diagram prompts) — https://github.com/dwzhu-pku/PaperBanana
  Licence: Apache License 2.0.
  How it is used: apps/api/app/services/paper_figure.py carries a short digest, rewritten in our
  own words, of the NeurIPS 2025 diagram style guide in that project's style_guides/ (pastel
  dashed regions, rounded process boxes, solid main flow, dashed side inputs and losses, one
  accent, no decoration). No PaperBanana code is included.

Univer (the spreadsheet grid of the 「시트」 surface) — https://univer.ai
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

@univerjs/presets, @univerjs/preset-sheets-core and the @univerjs/* packages they pull in
  Bundled into the web app (apps/web), pinned to 1.6.1; loaded only when a sheet is opened.
  Licence: Apache License 2.0 (the packages' own LICENSE files ship in node_modules/@univerjs/*).
  How it is used: the unmodified npm packages draw and edit a sheet in the browser. The
  community edition only; no Univer server, collaboration or paid plug-in is used, and the page
  makes no network call of Univer's (the app's content security policy would block one). The
  packages' own dependencies are all permissive: MIT, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, 0BSD and Apache-2.0.
